we want to load library class,
but not all his field, it's the pattern behind LAZY loading.
(we have library class that has composite relationship to Ebook
 but we want load library class without loading ebook class)

to implement it, we need a middle class as "proxy" class (EbookProxy)
between Library and Ebook. (it's act like agent
                            library just talk to proxy
                            ebook just talk to proxy)
we can put some logic on EbookProxy, that on just demand load Ebook!
this pattern used in many frameworks. (lazy loading)

1.create Ebooks interface that contain our
  main responsibility of books
  (we want all real and proxy have these functionalities)

2.the library just talk to proxy
  but due to flexibility, we use interface type in Library

3.just proxy can talk to real Ebook,
  (we create proxy to hide the real obj!)
  so we have real Ebook type in proxy.
  so we can pu some logic here, when a client want ebook
  proxy can do some process at this level (like make it lazy or logging)

Note: our implementation is following the open close principle,
      because tomorrow we can supply a different proxy implementation,
      like performs authorization or logging.
      we create new separate proxy (EbookLoggingProxy)
      we can just simply replace this new proxy that contain logging logic
      with old one, this is open close principle!

Note: in our example we had some code before calling the ebook (show() method)
      because we wanted to have lazy initialization,
      but that is not necessary as part of this pattern
      the whole point of this pattern is that this proxy is an object that
      look like a real subject, because both these classes implement the same interface
      (we we can implement another logic like logging,...)



